{"content":[{"c":["SHUR"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Wilderness region located in the Sinai Peninsula east of Egypt’s Nile Delta and west of the Negev. In antiquity, a caravan route passed through this region from Egypt to Palestine. Abraham lived for a time between Shur and Kadesh (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.20.1","r":"Gen.20.1","rawR":"Gen.20.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.20.1","value":"Gen.20.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 20:1"},"), and it was part of the territory occupied by the Ishmaelites (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.25.18","r":"Gen.25.18","rawR":"Gen.25.18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.25.18","value":"Gen.25.18"}],"t":"ref","v":"25:18"},"). After crossing the Red Sea, Moses led Israel on a three-day trek through this arid wasteland (",{"href":"?bref=Exod.15.22","r":"Exod.15.22","rawR":"Exod.15.22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.15.22","value":"Exod.15.22"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ex 15:22"},"). King Saul of Israel (1020–1000 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},") conquered the Amalekites in the vicinity of Shur (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.15.7","r":"1Sam.15.7","rawR":"1Sam.15.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.15.7","value":"1Sam.15.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 15:7"},"), and later David (1000–961 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},") defeated the Geshurites, Girzites, and Amalekites here (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.27.8","r":"1Sam.27.8","rawR":"1Sam.27.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.27.8","value":"1Sam.27.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"27:8"},"). The wilderness of Etham in ",{"href":"?bref=Num.33.8","r":"Num.33.8","rawR":"Num.33.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.33.8","value":"Num.33.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"Numbers 33:8"}," is identical with the wilderness of Shur."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=SinaSinai_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"SinaSinai_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"SinaSinai_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Sina, Sinai"},"; ",{"href":"?item=WildernessWanderings_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"WildernessWanderings_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"WildernessWanderings_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Wilderness Wanderings"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Shur","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 20:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.20.1","rawQueryValue":"Gen.20.1","sourceRefExact":"Gen.20.1"},{"anchorText":"25:18","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.25.18","rawQueryValue":"Gen.25.18","sourceRefExact":"Gen.25.18"},{"anchorText":"Ex 15:22","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Exod.15.22","rawQueryValue":"Exod.15.22","sourceRefExact":"Exod.15.22"},{"anchorText":"1 Sm 15:7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.15.7","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.15.7","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.15.7"},{"anchorText":"27:8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.27.8","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.27.8","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.27.8"},{"anchorText":"Numbers 33:8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.33.8","rawQueryValue":"Num.33.8","sourceRefExact":"Num.33.8"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"a924dcb8b255fe8273681bbfee7a1ca21e6614056863ee0afe42b84978ccac76","sourceItemName":"Shur","sourceItemOrder":391,"sourceMember":"Articles/S.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Shur","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Shur","title":"Shur","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}